{"author":{"id":"2de4467f26c42fb223f4d3ddd5611e7c0513d3daae4c1dc315de039036bc997d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1775413195,"nonce":"NI8boXVi2C25B8o+2os+4+CDsog=","title":"Wire ResponsiveImage as default img handler in MDX","message":"Standard markdown image syntax (`![alt](src)`) in MDX goes through `MdxImage`, which passes `src` verbatim. For raster images in folder-based posts, the originals are not copied to `public/` — only optimized AVIF/WebP variants exist (via `gen-images.mjs`). This means `![alt](/content/posts/slug/photo.jpg)` 404s in static export.\n\nFix: replace the `img` override in `mdx-content.tsx` with a component that checks the image manifest. Raster images found in the manifest get `\u003cpicture\u003e` tags with AVIF/WebP srcsets. SVGs and unknown images delegate to `MdxImage` (client component) for dark-mode switching and fallback.\n\nThis unblocks folder-based posts with co-located images.","files":null}]}